discimagestudio-linux is an independent Linux GUI frontend for
DiscImageStudio. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the
upstream DiscImageStudio project.

Upstream project: DiscImageStudio by JiaFeiMiao-K-Cat
(https://github.com/JiaFeiMiao-K-Cat/DiscImageStudio), licensed
under the GNU General Public License v3.0.

The frontend drives the official DiscImageStudio command-line
program as a subprocess (solve / simulate / selftest) and renders
none of the disc mathematics itself. Calibration drives the
separate disc-probe tool, also as a subprocess.

This project is licensed under the GNU General Public License
v3.0; see the LICENSE file.

Vendored components
-------------------
This repository vendors its two backends so a checkout is
self-contained. Both are unmodified.

official/ — the official DiscImageStudio CLI v1.5.0 (linux-x64)
binary from the upstream release tarball
DiscImageStudio-CLI-v1.5.0-linux-x64.tar.gz, with the tarball's
LICENSE and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt. Provenance and sha256
hashes are recorded in official/VERSION.json; the tarball hash
matches upstream's published SHA256SUMS.txt for v1.5.0.

probe/ — disc-probe by bczhc (https://github.com/bczhc/disc-probe),
GPL-3.0, vendored from commit
e0a07fd9bdaf63dac5adcf161c72218df4cafb4c. The photo gallery
under docs/showcase (22 MB) is omitted; see the upstream
repository for it. Files added by this project: fit_cubic.py,
phase_fit*.py, cmp_sectors.py, compare_models.py, and the
preset-*.json geometry presets.
